    "chunk_text": "AmCham Sri Lanka and Wijeya Newspapers to host Farzana Baduel for strategic communications forum\n\nHigh-level dialogue on reshaping Sri Lanka\u2019s global narrative for investment, talent, and international partnerships on 15 December at Taj Samudra, Colombo\n\nThe American Chamber of Commerce in Sri Lanka (AmCham SL), in partnership with Wijeya Newspapers Ltd., has announced a strategic forum titled, \u201cNarrating Sri Lanka\u2019s Story: How Strategic Communications Can Fuel Investment, Talent and Global Partnerships.\u201d The event will take place on 15 December 2025, from 10:00 a.m. to 11:30 a.m. at the Taj Samudra Colombo, followed by networking and refreshments.\n\nAs Sri Lanka works toward sustainable economic stabilisation and future-oriented growth, the need for a unified, credible, and compelling national narrative is more critical than ever. This forum will gather leading voices from global communications, business, investment, and policy to explore how the country can more effectively convey its strengths, ambitions, and opportunities to international audiences. In an era where nations compete not only on economic performance but also on perception, trust, and storytelling, this dialogue offers a timely and important platform.\n\nAmCham SL and Wijeya Newspapers Ltd., will host Curzon PR (UK) CEO and Co-Founder and Chartered Institute of Public Relations (CIPR UK), President-Elect Farzana Baduel as the keynote speaker."
  },
