    "chunk_text": "As Sri Lanka works toward sustainable economic stabilisation and future-oriented growth, the need for a unified, credible, and compelling national narrative is more critical than ever. This forum will gather leading voices from global communications, business, investment, and policy to explore how the country can more effectively convey its strengths, ambitions, and opportunities to international audiences. In an era where nations compete not only on economic performance but also on perception, trust, and storytelling, this dialogue offers a timely and important platform.\n\nAmCham SL and Wijeya Newspapers Ltd., will host Curzon PR (UK) CEO and Co-Founder and Chartered Institute of Public Relations (CIPR UK), President-Elect Farzana Baduel as the keynote speaker.\n\nFollowing the keynote, a thought-provoking panel discussion will explore how strategic communications can drive:\n\nDentsu Grant Group Chairperson and Managing Director; AmCham SL Director, Neela Marikkar\n\nBoard of Investment (BOI) Sri Lanka Director General Renuka Weerakone\n\nFirst Capital Holdings PLC Managing Director and CEO Dilshan Wirasekara\n\nThe session will be moderated by, The Sun (Daily Mirror) Editor, HI!! Online Editor, and Wijeya Newspapers Ltd., Head of Social Media Rishini Weeraratne.\n\nTogether, the panellists bring decades of experience in global markets, brand-building, and promoting Sri Lanka internationally. Their discussion will demonstrate how a cohesive national narrative can unlock new economic opportunities, strengthen investor confidence, and position Sri Lanka as a compelling destination for business, innovation, and skilled talent. Attendees can expect practical insights into aligning organisational messaging with national priorities, communicating purpose and credibility, and using storytelling as a competitive advantage."
