    "chunk_size_bytes": 1734,
    "chunk_text": "However, October 7 and Netanyahu\u2019s genocidal aggression in its aftermath flipped the long-flogged Jews (\u201cDavid\u201d) vs. Arabs (\u201cGoliath\u201d) false narrative. They confirmed the grotesque reality well known for decades among the non-West Global Majority (87%): the combined US-NATO-Israel behemoth (\u201cGoliath\u201d) is at war against the diminutive Palestine (\u201cDavid\u201d).\n\nConservative, pro-Israel podcasters routinely sought to limit the damage; they intimidated guests on their show, demanding: \u201cdo you condemn Hamas for October 7?\u201d The more perceptive observers not only limited their condemnation to the deliberate killing of civilians by either side; they also reached back to Frantz Fanon\u2019s analyses, in his Wretched of the Earth, of the role of violence in emancipating the colonised mind. They defended Hamas\u2019 Resistance as the necessary defensive violence by colonised Palestinians against the aggressive Israeli settler-colonialism.\n\nThe ANC leader Nelson Mandela\u2019s dialectical approach to Resistance, in his Long Walk to Freedom, encapsulates the logic of the Palestinian movement for self-determination: \u201cit is the oppressor who defines the nature of the struggle, and the oppressed is often left no recourse but to use methods that mirror those of the oppressor. At a point, one can only fight fire with fire.\u201d He contextualised non-violence not as an immutable, lofty principle but as a strategy, contingent upon the violence inflicted by the oppressor.\n\nLiberals often fail to grasp this nuanced view and impute a false equivalence between the violence of aggression and the violence of resistance (as in the interventions by Peace, Conflict Resolution and Policy Alternative \u201cactivists\u201d in Lanka)."
  },
