    "chunk_size_bytes": 1958,
    "chunk_text": "Mark and Comm named Rest of South Asia PR Agency of the Year 2025\n\nMark and Comm, Sri Lanka\u2019s leading boutique public relations and communications agency, has been honored at Campaign\u2019s Agency of the Year Awards 2025 (South Asia), taking home a Silver award and emerging as the sole agency in the Rest of South Asia PR Agency of the Year category. The ceremony took place on December 2 at the ITC Maratha in Mumbai.\n\nThe Campaign Asia-Pacific Agency of the Year Awards is the region\u2019s most prestigious recognition of excellence in advertising, marketing, and communications. Judged by leading client marketers, the awards celebrate outstanding achievements across creative, media, digital, PR, and specialized categories.\n\n\u201cThis recognition is a testament to our team\u2019s unwavering commitment to delivering PR-led strategies that drive real results for our clients,\u201d said Thanzyl Thajudeen, managing director of Mark and Comm. \u201cBeing the only agency shortlisted speaks volumes about the caliber of work we\u2019ve been producing where we create authentic connections that resonate with diverse audiences.\u201d\n\nEstablished in 2011, Mark and Comm has evolved into a strategic PR consultancy for leading local and multinational brands across technology, agriculture, apparel, FMCG, finance and insurance, hospitality, education, mobility, and sustainability sectors. The agency\u2019s boutique model emphasizes strategic counsel and agile execution, delivering integrated communications solutions.\n\nMark and Comm\u2019s global reach is amplified through strategic international affiliations. The agency is a member of the GlobalCom PR Network, joining over 80 independent PR agencies operating across more than 100 countries worldwide. Additionally, the agency maintains non-exclusive affiliations with two leading global PR agencies, and is a corporate member of the PRCA APAC, with Thajudeen serving on the PRCA APAC Board and CIPR International Committee."
