    "description": "EDB launches fast-track relief to support exporters affected by adverse weather",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/EDB-launches-fast-track-relief-to-support-exporters-affected-by-adverse-weather/34-785399",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1765241635.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-12-09-dailyftlk-bfe0d99a-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "6818b8dfaf6f905835d467eb7221841c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 895,
    "chunk_text": "The EDB is currently working closely with customs, port authorities, and logistics providers to manage infrastructure delays caused by adverse weather conditions and expedite export-related clearances.\n\nThe discussion highlighted the growing intensity and frequency of climate-related challenges in recent times, underscoring the urgent need for proactive and sustainable responses. It was emphasised that addressing these environmental issues is not only critical for mitigating risks but also essential for ensuring long-term economic resilience. By integrating sustainability into export practices and promoting green technologies, the EDB aims to strengthen the export sector\u2019s competitiveness and sustainability. This approach seeks to support exporters in adapting to climate realities while fostering greener and more resilient trade pathways that align with global environmental goals."
  },
