    "chunk_size_bytes": 1861,
    "chunk_text": "Construction sector fuels rally as CSE surges past 22,000 points\n\nThe Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE) witnessed a robust trading session yesterday, propelled notably by the construction sector. The All Share Price Index (ASPI) closed sharply higher, exceeding the 22,000-point milestone amidst healthy turnover levels. Broad-based buying interest was evident as most sectors advanced.\n\nMarket activity was dominated by\u00a0Tokyo Cement Company,\u00a0Access Engineering PLC, and Colombo Dockyard PLC.\n\nSignificant crossings were also recorded in several key counters, including\u00a0Tokyo Cement Company (Lanka) PLC,\u00a0Lanka Glass PLC,\u00a0Richard Pieris & Company PLC,\u00a0Sierra Cables PLC,\u00a0C. T. Land Development PLC, and\u00a0Hemas Holdings PLC.\n\nNotably, trading in Tokyo Cement Company alone contributed to approximately 8% of the day\u2019s total turnover, underscoring the intense investor focus on construction-related stocks. The session remained busy throughout largely driven by this sectoral momentum.\n\nConsequently, the turnover stood at Rs 3.8 billion with nine crossings. Those seven crossings were reported in ACL Cables 300,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 75.5 million and its share price traded at Rs 255, Tokyo Cement 500,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 51 million and its share price traded at Rs 102, Laughs Gas 658,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 42.1 million and its share price traded at Rs 53.10, Richard Pieris one million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 41 million and its share price traded at Rs 40, Sierra Cables 1.2 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 40 million and its share price traded at Rs 40, RIL Properties one million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 31.5\u00a0 \u00a0million and its share price traded at Rs 31.50 and Cables Solutions\u00a0 1.5 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 31.7 million and its share price traded at Rs 14.50."
