    "chunk_text": "Aberdeen Holdings\u2019 Group Companies honored at Presidential Environment Awards 2025\n\nAberdeen Holdings, a diversified conglomerate operating across seven industries in Sri Lanka, continues to demonstrate its commitment to sustainability and responsible business practices across all its subsidiaries. This dedication was recognized at the 11th\u00a0Annual Presidential Environment Awards 2025, held on 23rd\u00a0October 2025 at BMICH under the patronage of Anura Kumara Dissanayake, President of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka. Three of the Group\u2019s companies \u2013 Neptune Papers (Pvt) Ltd, Ex-Pack Corrugated Cartons PLC, and Ruhunu Farms (Pvt) Ltd were honored among the nation\u2019s leading contributors to environmental excellence.\n\nNeptune Papers (Pvt) Ltd received the Silver Award for its leadership in recycling and advancing Sri Lanka\u2019s circular economy. A long-standing pioneer in large-scale waste recovery segment, Neptune continues to transform waste into economic opportunity while promoting employment generation, reducing landfill dependency, and driving circular economy. The award was accepted by Fazleen Majeed, Chief Executive Officer of Neptune Papers, in recognition of the company\u2019s continued contribution to building a cleaner and more resource-efficient Sri Lanka.\n\nEx-Pack Corrugated Cartons PLC received a Merit Award for its consistent commitment to sustainability and responsible manufacturing. As a Carbon Neutral and WRAP-certified company, Ex-Pack has embedded ESG principles into its operations, setting a benchmark for environmentally conscious manufacturing in Sri Lanka\u2019s packaging sector. The award was accepted by Azhar Sheriff, Head of Compliance and Sustainability of Ex-Pack Corrugated Cartons, marking another milestone in the company\u2019s journey toward a more sustainable future."
