    "md5": "cd1d07016a751ac27fd6f6ce3f70d3a2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1981,
    "chunk_text": "IMM snatches victory for Sri Lanka at ASOCIO Awards 2025\n\nInclusive Media Monitoring (Pvt) Ltd. (IMM) has snatched a historic victory for Sri Lanka, clinching the coveted ASOCIO Outstanding Digital Transformation Organization Award at a glittering ceremony held on November 7 in Taipei, Taiwan.\n\nThe Asian-Oceanian Computing Industry Organization (ASOCIO) is the premier ICT industry body in the Asia-Pacific region. Founded in 1984 and headquartered in Tokyo, ASOCIO represents more than 24,000 technology companies across 24 member economies, including Japan, Korea, Singapore, Australia, India, Malaysia, and now proudly Sri Lanka through its member federation FITIS. Known as the \u201cOscars of Asian digital excellence,\u201d the annual ASOCIO Awards recognise organisations that demonstrate exceptional leadership in digital innovation and transformation.\n\nThis triumph puts Sri Lanka firmly on the regional digital map and underscores IMM\u2019s leadership in delivering world-class ad verification, social media monitoring, and electronic media monitoring services. In an era where data drives decisions, IMM has emerged as the homegrown champion empowering Sri Lankan businesses to compete\u2014and win\u2014on a level playing field with global players.\n\n\u201cWe didn\u2019t just attend the ASOCIO Awards \u2013 we came, we showcased Sri Lankan ingenuity, and we snatched the top honour,\u201d said Jayantha Sittampalam, Managing Director of Inclusive Media Monitoring (Pvt) Ltd. \u201cThis victory belongs to every Sri Lankan organisation that believes local innovation can lead Asia. Our new all-in-one dashboard is proof: from Colombo to the world stage, we are transforming how businesses track performance, verify ads, and outsmart competitors.\u201d\n\nThe centrepiece of IMM\u2019s award-winning transformation is its revolutionary all-in-one dashboard \u2013 a powerful, unified platform that allows organisations to monitor their own performance alongside every competitor in their sector in real time."
