    "chunk_size_bytes": 890,
    "chunk_text": "Colombo-based diplomats make Rs. 3.6 m personal contribution to \u2018Rebuilding Sri Lanka\u2019 Fund\n\nDiplomats based in Colombo have made a personal contribution of Rs. 3.6 million to the government\u2019s \u201cRebuilding Sri Lanka\u201d Fund, which provides relief to people affected by the recent devastating cyclone.\n\nThe relevant cheque was handed over yesterday to Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath, by Ambassador of Indonesia Dewi Gustina Tobing.\n\nJoining the occasion were several Ambassadors and High Commissioners representing their countries based in Colombo, including Ambassador of South Korea Lee Miyon, Ambassador of Switzerland Dr. Siri Walt, Ambassador of Palestine Ihab I.M. Khalil, High Commissioner of the Maldives Masood Imad, Charge d\u2019 Affaires, Embassy of Oman Said Al Harbi and Deputy Head of Mission, Embassy of Italy Alberto Arcidiacono."
  },
