    "language": "en",
    "md5": "821b5ed6b3e199576024615627a34f05",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1906,
    "chunk_text": "AKD says Sri Lanka remains grateful for support extended by US and other friendly nations\n\nVisiting US Under Secretary of State for Political Affairs Allison Hooker calls on President Dissanayake\n\nExpresses confidence in Sri Lanka\u2019s recovery under President Dissanayake\u2019s leadership\n\nThe visiting US Under Secretary of State for Political Affairs Allison Hooker yesterday expressed her confidence in President Anura Kumara Dissanayake\u2019s leadership in steering Sri Lanka\u2019s recovery and rebuilding efforts.\n\nDuring a courtesy call on President Dissanayake, she affirmed that the United States stands ready to provide any necessary support to assist Sri Lanka\u2019s recovery.\n\nHooker also conveyed her condolences to the families of the victims of the disaster and expressed satisfaction at being able to extend assistance during this challenging period.\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake conveyed his appreciation for the assistance provided by the President of the United States and the government in dispatching various relief teams to the country during this challenging period. The President also acknowledged the sincere support offered to Sri Lanka by all friendly nations globally, including the United States.\n\nPresident Dissanayake highlighted that Sri Lanka encountered this disaster while the nation\u2019s economy was on the path to stabilisation and economic indicators were showing improvement. He emphasised the need for future focus on enhancing the livelihoods of those affected and on the long-term development of infrastructure facilities.\n\nThe President stated that restoring infrastructure, including highways and railways, as well as key income sources such as agriculture, livestock and small to medium-sized enterprises, which have been devastated by floods and landslides, will require time. He also expressed the expectation of support from all friendly nations in this effort."
  },
