    "chunk_text": "Position Sri Lanka as a regional leader in wellness, Ayurveda, meditation retreats, and integrative health tourism.\n\nUpgrade domestic airports and introduce low-cost inter-regional air connectivity (Mattala\u2013Koggala\u2013Sigiriya\u2013Batticaloa).\n\nIdentify 10\u201312 tourism development zones (East Coast, North, Tea Country, Wildlife Belt, Cultural Triangle, and lesser-known coastal towns).\n\nCreate investment-friendly clusters offering land banks, tax incentives, infrastructure support, and streamlined approvals.\n\nTourism investors, especially SMEs and mid-sized hotel owners, must be safeguarded from systemic shocks.\n\nCreate a dedicated Tourism Revival Bank or fund for refinancing, upgrading, and expansion.\n\nOffer tax incentives for renovations, sustainability upgrades, and skill training.\n\nEstablish a Tourism Ombudsman for fair dispute resolution between banks and investors.\n\nA unified national booking and information platform\u2014powered by real-time data\u2014featuring experiences, transport, festivals, and local businesses.\n\nMandatory digital training for tourism SMEs to improve online presence, pricing, and customer engagement.\n\nUse data analytics for demand forecasting, promotional targeting, and crisis response.\n\nEnforce sustainable development standards for hotels, ensuring waste, energy, and water efficiency.\n\nDevelop protected wildlife corridors and regulated safari models to prevent overcrowding at national parks.\n\nnIntroduce a national certification framework for guides, drivers, and tourism service providers.\n\nSri Lanka\u203as global presence must be bold, strategic, and consistent.\n\nYear-long digital campaigns targeting Europe, India, China, the Middle East, and emerging markets.\n\nCollaborations with airlines, influencers, film producers, and global travel platforms.\n\nPromote megaprojects such as events tourism, sports tourism, MICE, and cruise tourism."
