    "chunk_size_bytes": 1665,
    "chunk_text": "Venerable Mettavihari Thera\n\nVen. Mettavihari is no more. I messaged Ven Vajiraramaye Nanaseeha Thera last week to find out what information he had on Ven Mettavihari. I knew he had gone home to Denmark to have a further operation as he had had colon cancer. Ven Nanaseeha said he had not heard from him. Then two hours later, he shared a letter he had received from Ven Mettavihari\u2019s brother to say the Bhikkhu had died. The Ajahn Brahm Society, the late monk was advisor/patron of, also gave me the very sad news.\n\nI got to know Ven Mettavihari from at least two decades ago since he resided in the Narada Dharmayathana temple off Buller\u2019s Road (now Bauddhaloka Mawatha) and I would take morning dane on every 25th of each month. Venerables Mettavihari and Dhammavihari resided in this Centre and once, one of them joked I was getting tied up in Vihari names. I would take fruit juice, cornflakes etc in deference to this Western monk.\n\nI well remember going to the temple with a niece when her brother was terminally ill, so the patient could hear pirit chanted before the very end. A gentleman who wanted the head monk to speak with some people would not be put off although our need was urgent. Ven Dhammavihari, who was just after an eye lens replacement, said he would come with Ven Mettavihari joining him to the private hospital, not at all minding going so soon after surgery and traveling with two women, one driving the car.\n\nOn another occasion he came with me to see my brother who was after a mild stroke to speak with him. My brother asked him how his wife was. Replied the monk with a broad smile \u201cI have no wife.\u201d He had renounced his all."
  },
  {
