    "chunk_size_bytes": 1510,
    "chunk_text": "He introduced me to the Ajahn Brahm Society which he formed with a couple of devoted and modern-thinking young persons who invited and arranged the visits to Sri Lanka of Ajahn Brahmavamso and Ajahn Brahmali from Perth, Australia. Thousands of lay persons and hundreds of bhikkhus and bhikkhunis benefitted from their talks and medication retreats. Because I wrote a couple of articles for the Society, led by Ven Mettavihari, its members came to thank me with a huge cake!\n\nOnce I was unwell with flu and could not attend a meeting. The next day he walked all the way to my home to see me. That was a measure of his concern.\n\nHe would walk barefoot whatever time of day. He once got seriously ill due to an infection caught thus. Ven Dhammavihari moved urgently to his rescue, as he had done earlier when he saw the bhikkhu panting each time he climbed a flight of stairs. He saved the bhikkhu since he was developing heart trouble.\n\nAnd so this gracious, self giving, so helpful and concerned Ven Mettavihari is no more. We need not wish him a speedy Nibbana because he is very close to that wonderful state of no more births, deaths and suffering.\n\n\u201cWhen Justice Steps In: The Supreme Court Breaks the Cycle of Ragging Impunity\u201d\n\nMinister Athulathmudali\u2019s skill and application at the Ministry of Agriculture\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
