    "chunk_size_bytes": 1971,
    "chunk_text": "Venerable Denm\u0101rkaye Mett\u0101vih\u0101ri Mah\u0101 Thera\n\nIt was only a few months back, on July 27, 2025, to be precise, that a letter was prepared and handed over to Venerable Mett\u00e2vih\u00e2ri Mah\u00e2 Thera by Most Venerable Tirikunamale Ananda Mahanayaka Thera recommending a short respite in Denmark. This was when Ven. Mett\u00e2vih\u00e2ri Mah\u00e2 Thera expressed his wish to return to Denmark for treatment.\n\nI have known late Ven. Mett\u00e2vih\u00e2ri for over four decades when both of us were laymen and have even visited the beautiful house he built with his spouse, a Sri Lankan. who by profession was an architect. It was a storied building near Asok\u00e2r\u00e2ma temple, facing Havelock Road, Colombo 5, and the rooftop of their house was a beautiful garden open to the skies. That was my first experience of a rooftop garden, which was not a very common sight those days.\n\nVen. Mett\u00e2vih\u00e2ri\u2019s lay name was Joergen Jacob Sylvest Jakobsen. His parents, Helmer and Dagmar, had five children and Jacob was the second in his family. Born on February 21, 1945, he came to Sri Lanka in 1969 when he was 24 years of age. Before long he got married and led a fruitful married life with his Sri Lankan wife for 18 years, after which both decided to renounce worldly life and devote their lives to the Dhamma. In 1988 he received ordination with the Most Ven Madihe Pannasiha Mahanayaka Thera as preceptor and Ven. Ampitiye Sri Rahula Maha Thera as teacher; and so was his spouse.\n\nHe was a very pious, unassuming monk and it was a common sight to see him walking barefoot on a tarred road from the Narada Centre, at Sarana Road off Bauddhaloka Mawatha, where he later chose to reside. He was a computer expert and he profitably used his computer knowledge in good stead within the resources he had. I was a lay person then and was a frequent visitor to the Narada Centre to assist him in his work. I like to mention with gratitude that I was initiated to using email and to the computer world by him."
  },
