    "chunk_text": "He was a very pious, unassuming monk and it was a common sight to see him walking barefoot on a tarred road from the Narada Centre, at Sarana Road off Bauddhaloka Mawatha, where he later chose to reside. He was a computer expert and he profitably used his computer knowledge in good stead within the resources he had. I was a lay person then and was a frequent visitor to the Narada Centre to assist him in his work. I like to mention with gratitude that I was initiated to using email and to the computer world by him.\n\nA very valuable contribution of his was the digitalizing of the Tipitaka, the Pali Canon, on the initiative of Most Venerable Madihe Pannasiha Mahanayaka Thera, his preceptor. The Tipitaka is available for free download in three languages from his website metta.lk. One of his close Dhamma friends was late Venerable Dhammavihari Maha Thera, who was Professor of Pali and Buddhist Studies and one-time Editor of the Buddhist Encyclopaedia. They were both resident monks of the Narada Centre that was once called the Buddhist Information and Research Centre under the directorship of Ven. Dhammavih\u00e2ri Maha Thera. Ven. Mett\u00e2vih\u00e2ri assisted him in the preparation and production of the second edition of Buddhist Monastic Discipline authored by Ven. Dhammavihari. His heart was always open to help others and he was ever ready to use his technological know-how in the service of the Dhamma."
