    "chunk_size_bytes": 1843,
    "chunk_text": "Sinopec supports flood-hit communities with emergency relief\n\nSinopec has mobilized to support relief efforts by donating 75,000\u202fLitres of bottled drinking water to flood affected regions. The initiative was launched nationwide through Sinopec\u2019s Filling Stations Network located in areas deeply impacted by the disaster. With many parts of the country facing disruptions to essential services, access to safe drinking water has emerged as a priority need.\n\nAfter ensuring uninterrupted fuel supply to its Filling Station network, Sinopec responded swiftly to the national emergency by activating its flagship CSR programme, Clear Spring, to deliver drinking water to communities in need. Distribution was carried out through filling stations and strategic partners in several of the hardest hit regions, including Kandy, Badulla, Arachchikattu, Anuradhapura, Jaffna, Biyagama, Kaduwela and Kelaniya. In addition, water donations were delivered directly to the offices of the Kandy District Secretariat, Gampola Youth Centre, Kurunegala local government and Pudukkudiyiruppu Divisional Secretariat, supporting broader public sector relief and recovery efforts.\n\nThe donation drive took on added significance when Kumar Jayakody, Minister of Energy, personally joined Sinopec staff and volunteers in Biyagama to distribute water packages to flood affected families. The presence of government officials, together with the voluntary efforts of Sinopec\u2019s staff who mobilised without hesitation, underscored the collaborative spirit of public institutions and private operators in the Energy sectors working together to respond to a national crisis.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
