    "chunk_size_bytes": 903,
    "chunk_text": "Almas Holdings commits Rs. 250 m to \u2018Rebuilding Sri Lanka\u2019 Fund\n\nAlmas Holdings Ltd. has made a financial contribution of Rs. 100 million to the Government\u2019s \u2018Rebuilding Sri Lanka\u2019 Fund, established to provide relief to communities affected by the Ditwah cyclone.\n\nThe cheque was handed over at the Presidential Secretariat by Almas Holdings Chairman Imtiaz Buhardeen to Secretary to the President Dr. Nandika Sanath Kumanayake. The company has pledged an additional Rs. 150 million.\n\nDuring the meeting, Buhardeen expressed the company\u2019s commitment to extend further support for flood relief and reconstruction initiatives in the Kandy District.\n\nAlso present on the occasion were Almas Equities Managing Director Shameer Buhardeen, Directors Risvi Abdul Majeed and Ruzly Shamsudeen, Almas Equities CEO Ifadh Marikar and Almas Holdings Strategic Development Advisor of Takshila Hulangamuwa."
  },
