    "chunk_size_bytes": 1883,
    "chunk_text": "Unscrambling Eggs\n\nThis colorful expression was introduced into the local lexicon by that brilliant mind and oratorical skill of Dr Colvin. R. De Silva. I do not recall the exact context which prompted this gem. It could have been the Land Reform or the Ceiling on Housing Bill. Both were controversial, and this was in effect, a jibe at those opposed to this \u201creformatory\u201d legislation. In my opinion there are two other examples of willfully scrambled eggs. These are:\n\n(i) The drastic interference by banning imports of Agrochemicals (fertilizers and pesticides), and the imports of Palm oil, both \u201cwith immediate effect.\u201d\n\nThe first stupidity led to a severe depletion of returns to already poor farmers, and In turn led to serious defaults on Bank Loans, and disastrous escalation of living costs. These nearly catastrophic consequences, could at least be rectified in a season or two.\n\nNot so with the second, (National Languages Bill) imposition. This was essentially a fraudulent exercise and a colossal deception. It was quite unworthy of the supposed brilliance and nationalist conscience of the principal proponent of this abomination, (then PM) Mr SWRD Bandaranaike, who meanwhile ensured that his own children were educated overseas, and in English.\n\nAlong with this, the children of the other privileged few, too were thus able to enjoy the superior benefits on offer at prestigious schools and Universities abroad. Meanwhile, gullible people were led by empty promises of a national revival and a crowning glory of \u201cThe Common Man.\u201d Prudence would dictate that reputable Universities should rather serve the prestige and efforts of the \u201cUncommon Man.\u201d\n\nNot only is this negative goal of pretended \u201cequality\u201d fraudulent, it also commits the crime of wrecking the futures of the large majority of under-endowed and much impoverished strata of society."
  },
  {
