    "md5": "d67fab395c858bfba87dc1938fdbf7ff",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1957,
    "chunk_text": "Along with this, the children of the other privileged few, too were thus able to enjoy the superior benefits on offer at prestigious schools and Universities abroad. Meanwhile, gullible people were led by empty promises of a national revival and a crowning glory of \u201cThe Common Man.\u201d Prudence would dictate that reputable Universities should rather serve the prestige and efforts of the \u201cUncommon Man.\u201d\n\nNot only is this negative goal of pretended \u201cequality\u201d fraudulent, it also commits the crime of wrecking the futures of the large majority of under-endowed and much impoverished strata of society.\n\nThere could only be a miniscule, about 12 or 13 million Sinhala speakers in a world population of 7,000 million. it is an absurdity beyond compare, to believe that in this world, the \u201cSinhala only\u201c bunch will have survival chances even as long as those of a snowball in hell.\n\nEven ignoring the fact that language is primarily a tool of communication between persons and bluffing the gullible, tying up cultural and religious issues, and thus presenting a false narrative, linking language to cultural and sovereignty issues. It thereby became possible to entangle a deceived populace, to a disastrously emotive and false pretext of cultural, sovereignty.\n\nWe may also remind ourselves that we humans are as the only known species that has developed the ability to communicate vocally and by writing, with others of our fellow members. There must surely be divine or evolutionary purposes for this unique ability, which it wold be perilous to abandon. Our plight proves this reality.\n\nWhy was the free will and democratic fundamental right of a parent, to decide on the language of instruction of his child? The truth is that it was a diabolical way of a despicable strategy, to deprive children of Sinhala and Tamil parentage to a subordinate position, while retaining this privilege for the community of which the then Minister belonged."
  },
