    "md5": "732c8fd5d41c1881d4089a79e82e33ea",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1249,
    "chunk_text": "Why was the free will and democratic fundamental right of a parent, to decide on the language of instruction of his child? The truth is that it was a diabolical way of a despicable strategy, to deprive children of Sinhala and Tamil parentage to a subordinate position, while retaining this privilege for the community of which the then Minister belonged.\n\nRecently, the point was made that minister Suni Handuneththi, embarrassed himself by his faltering pronunciation at an international event. This continuing evil, brought back memories of a Minister, who had nominated himself to attend an important technical assembly, at CERN, (The International Centre for Nuclear Research). The poor fellow was a lawyer by training, and so was completely beyond his depth as would be a \u201cfish out of water,\u201d or a Daniel tossed into a Lion\u2019s Den.\n\nThe price that our nation has foolishly squandered in the formal pursuit of an evident hypocrisy, and created the certainty that a community may well be subject to future violence.\n\nHere is an egg so comprehensively scrambled, that it has rotted to a degree where no miracle will be capable of delivering eggs, so that we may scramble them yet again. Stupidity, like History, has a way of repeating itself."
