    "md5": "d2cb6ecae82463e64e7dba508e6ffd71",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1514,
    "chunk_text": "Anura Is A Clever Man, Is He?\n\nI recently watched a political discussion between my friends Shiral Lakthilaka\u00a0and KW Janaranjana, the editor of Anidda, a weekly alternative newspaper.\n\nI watched a different political chat between Professor Jayadeva Uyangoda and Professor Nirmal Ranjith Dewasiri last week, but it was qualitatively very poor and biased, compared to this discussion. Therefore, I found it worthy of evaluating the discussion between Shiral and Janaranjana. Please watch this YouTube video!\n\nI would agree with Shiral to a reasonable extent, but there are also some matters that I will not be able to comply with him.\u00a0 Let me first outline some of his positive and correct observations, leaving to discuss disagreeable matters later.\n\n1. Shiral directly attacks one of the false fabrications that JVP/NPP cadres have been deliberately disseminating. As most people know, those party cadres try to explain the victory of the Malimawa as a turning point in Sri Lankan society, which marked the end of the era ruled by the elite and beginning of a new period of the common man. Shiral denies this lie with disgust. As everyone knows, the electoral victory in 1956 marked this turning point. This social transformation was confirmed by the non-elite leaders like Dahanayake, Premadasa, Wijetunga and Sirisena, who succeeded in ascending to power.\u00a0 Even the Rajapaksas were not fully pledged elites like the members of the Senanayake, Kotelawala, Bandaranaike, Jayewardene and Wickremesinghe families."
  },
