    "chunk_size_bytes": 1755,
    "chunk_text": "1. Shiral directly attacks one of the false fabrications that JVP/NPP cadres have been deliberately disseminating. As most people know, those party cadres try to explain the victory of the Malimawa as a turning point in Sri Lankan society, which marked the end of the era ruled by the elite and beginning of a new period of the common man. Shiral denies this lie with disgust. As everyone knows, the electoral victory in 1956 marked this turning point. This social transformation was confirmed by the non-elite leaders like Dahanayake, Premadasa, Wijetunga and Sirisena, who succeeded in ascending to power.\u00a0 Even the Rajapaksas were not fully pledged elites like the members of the Senanayake, Kotelawala, Bandaranaike, Jayewardene and Wickremesinghe families.\n\n3. Shiral observes the nature of the so-called internal democracy that the JVP and its affiliated organisations function through. He simply highlights how the inter-university federation leaders make decisions without consulting representatives of various student segments, political and non-political.\n\nlet me point out some matters that I will not be able to comply with Shiral.\n\n1. Shiral says that Anura is capable of balancing Sinhala and Tamil nationalisms more effectively, without jeopardising the government\u2019s popularity among both the communities. According to him, Anura is a clever man. In English, there are so many synonyms for cleverness, i.e., smart, shrewd, genius, witty, tricky, cunning and some other words, even though their meanings sometimes overlap. Certainly, Anura is a clever man, but his cleverness is much closer to that of opportunistic Makandure Madush. Anyway, this act of deceiving is temporary; Anura will see the consequences of his dirty tactic shortly."
