    "chunk_text": "1. Shiral says that Anura is capable of balancing Sinhala and Tamil nationalisms more effectively, without jeopardising the government\u2019s popularity among both the communities. According to him, Anura is a clever man. In English, there are so many synonyms for cleverness, i.e., smart, shrewd, genius, witty, tricky, cunning and some other words, even though their meanings sometimes overlap. Certainly, Anura is a clever man, but his cleverness is much closer to that of opportunistic Makandure Madush. Anyway, this act of deceiving is temporary; Anura will see the consequences of his dirty tactic shortly.\n\n4. Shiral sometimes uses technical terms in politics unscrupulously.\u00a0 For instance, the terms like middleclass, deduction theory, Bonapartism and state capitalism have no clearcut definitions; they have to be applied very\u00a0 carefully to avoid the emergence of wrong connotations. For Shiral, the system existed under Sirima Bandaranaike also comes under the designation called state capitalism, even though there was a national capitalist class comprised of indigenous businesspersons during that regime. His prudent political knowledge fails to detect the difference between Singapore or China, where the state capitalism has prevailed and the countries like Sri Lanka or India, where the mixed economic system existed in the past. He follows the same manner in regard with other terms as well.\n\n5. Shiral assumes that there is a liberal movement and a liberal class in Sri Lanka. The reality is that this country has never had such a movement or a class other than a very thin social stratum, especially in urban areas. It seems that many people misunderstand neoliberalism as an extension of liberalism. Liberalism has nothing to do with neoliberalism; conservatives developed that extreme economic ideology, because conservatism was devoid of a proper system and a theory related to economics to be consistent with their regressive political doctrine."
