    "chunk_text": "8. Shiral then turns to prescribe for the current problem, that is, the rule of the inefficient JVP/NPP government. He attempts to find a substitution through the amalgamation of four forces or their leaders. According to him, there are five leaders, i.e., Ranil, Dilith, Namal, Sajith and Milinda Moragoda, who is out of the scene now. He prefers Ranil despite this mature leader\u2019s declared poor health condition.\u00a0But the reality is that the SJB led by Sajith cannot be cornered, if anybody wants to defeat the incumbent government. Meanwhile, Shiral has overlooked the Harini-factor, which apparently causes damage to the coherence of the government.\n\nFinally, it must be said that Janaranjana, who conducted the interview, has done a marvellous job, but he should and could have given a more perplexing task for Shiral, who came as the resource person."
