    "md5": "89a23601caae084a9a35d95d79a4c34d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1958,
    "chunk_text": "Suzi \u2026 missing Sri Lanka\n\nAlthough based in Switzerland, singer Suzi Fl\u00fcckiger (better known in the scene here as Suzi Croner), still calls her land of birth \u2026 \u201chome,\u201d and her mind is very much focused on Sri Lanka these days.\n\nShe had plans, she says, to travel to Colombo, mainly to spend Christmas with her loved ones, but she found her workload, in Switzerland, doubled, due to the festive period \u2026 and then came Cyclone Ditwah!\n\nSuzi went on to say that she is so saddened by what has taken place in Sri Lanka.\n\n\u201cI\u2019m hoping the recovery period will be short and normalcy will return soon.\u201d\n\nGenerally, her trips to Colombo are mainly to entertain her music lovers, fans and her friends, and she last visited the island, in September, this year, as a performer, and did her thing at a five-star venue for the Oktoberfest celebrations.\n\nAs usual, the crowd enjoyed her performance; Suzi is, indeed, a very entertaining artiste.\n\nSuzi is also a favourite with the crowd in Melbourne, Australia, and has already been booked to perform at a Valentine\u2019s Day event, in Melbourne, in February, 2026 \u2013 her fourth trip Down Under.\n\nWith the cyclone disaster in mind, Suzi indicated that she would love to do a fund-raiser, during her trip to Australia \u2026 if the possibilities are there.\n\nThe singer is very keen to checkout Sri Lanka, as soon as possible, and indicated she is now looking forward to coming this way, after her Australian trip.\n\nIn her home town of Switzerland, Suzi performs four nights a week and the scene, according to Suzi, gets hectic as Christmas and the dawning of the New Year gets closer.\n\n\u201cI will be doing special events on Christmas Eve, Christmas Day, and New Year\u2019s Eve.\u201d\n\nHowever, the day after Christmas, 26th December, she says she is going to have a Christmas party, at home, for her friends.\n\n\u201cThey keep worrying me for a party and so I thought \u2026let\u2019s have the get-together on 26th December.\u201d"
