    "md5": "3690d81c0f82f105e680e00db28f0dac",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1852,
    "chunk_text": "Pushpika Janadheera reappointed SLAMERP Chairman\n\nThe Sri Lanka Association of Manufacturers and Exporters of Rubber Products (SLAMERP) has reappointed Dipped Products PLC Managing Director Pushpika Janadheera, as its Chairman at the Association\u2019s 15th Annual General Meeting.\n\nSLAMERP is a leading industry body for Sri Lanka\u2019s value-added rubber products sector, which contributes $ 1 billion in export earnings while strengthening the country\u2019s position as a global supplier of high-quality rubber products. The Association represents manufacturers and exporters in the rubber sector, promotes market expansion, and supports efforts to improve global market access for Sri Lankan products. It also plays a key role in national policy dialogue on issues that influence the stability and long-term growth of the rubber industry.\n\nUnder Janadheera\u2019s leadership, SLAMERP has taken clear and proactive positions on challenges faced by the sector. The Association called for immediate Government engagement when the United States announced tariff on Sri Lankan rubber imports, a development that threatened export competitiveness and the livelihoods of thousands of families linked to the rubber value chain. SLAMERP also raised strong concerns regarding the proposed removal of the SVAT scheme, cautioning that the change would create severe cash-flow pressure for SMEs, and exporters unless a tested refund mechanism was in place.\n\nBeyond its advocacy efforts, SLAMERP continues to focus on strengthening local supply chains, increasing raw rubber production, and uplifting smallholder communities that form the foundation of the sector. The Association works closely with the Plantation Industries Ministry, and the Export Development Board to expand market access and support national export objectives aligned with Sri Lanka\u2019s 2030 roadmap."
  },
